WEBVTT

00:00:00.252 --> 00:00:02.000
Security conditions change over time.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.450
A system that was understood during authorization may later experience new

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.280
vulnerabilities,

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:11.335
architecture changes, user changes, dependency changes, incidents, policy updates,

00:00:11.335 --> 00:00:13.000
or shifts in mission importance.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.265
RMF emphasizes continuous monitoring so organizations can identify changes,

00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:20.000
evaluate control effectiveness, address emerging risks,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.280
and support informed decision making throughout system operation.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.335
Continuous monitoring may include vulnerability scanning, configuration monitoring,

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:32.000
log review, incident reporting, control assessments, access reviews, patch tracking,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
risk register updates, and review of plans of action.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.280
The goal is not to collect data for its own sake.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.280
Monitoring should help stakeholders understand whether controls remain effective,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.260
whether risk has changed, and whether new action is needed.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.000
Monitoring also supports accountability after authorization.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.000
If a system changes materially, if a control stops working,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.200
or if a high-risk finding remains open,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.000
leaders need current information to decide what to do next.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.960
A mature monitoring program connects technical signals to governance decisions.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.960
For example, vulnerability trends, failed control checks, delayed remediation,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.270
or repeated incidents can all become risk information.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.980
Continuous monitoring makes RMF an ongoing management practice rather than a static

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:09.917
approval package.

00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:13.415
It keeps the organization aware of current conditions and helps risk decisions evolve with

00:01:13.415 --> 00:01:14.000
the system.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
For operational teams, monitoring also creates early warning.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Current evidence can reveal control drift, delayed remediation, repeated weaknesses,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.000
or system changes that should be reviewed before they become larger issues.
